From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:08:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 171/194] hjviewer: the service's process tries the main pipe
 once more before it ends the window that holds it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The main window of an installed HJViewer whose service is stopped serves
the main pipe itself. Pressing 서비스 시작 in it starts the service, and
the service's process (--server, SYSTEM) comes up while that window
still holds the pipe: the window has yet to start the window and the
tray that replace it and end. The process could not bind the pipe,
ended the window at once and could leave the PC with a working service
and no window. Since the pipes are checked, the process can also no
longer ask such a window to close over the pipe (a SYSTEM client takes
no pipe a user owns), so ending it is all that is left. It now waits
one second and tries the pipe again, and only then ends the window as
before.

Backported from rustdesk/rustdesk 2228db8a1098f84e01577d983453e805cca3c3a1 (fix(windows): retry service IPC before terminating the GUI (#16913))
Upstream's diff applies unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/server.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/server.rs b/src/server.rs
index b8aed9f..8770231 100644
--- a/src/server.rs
+++ b/src/server.rs
@@ -683,6 +683,16 @@ pub async fn start_server(is_server: bool, no_server: bool) {
                 if let Err(err) = crate::ipc::start("") {
                     log::error!("Failed to start ipc: {}", err);
                     if crate::is_server() {
+                        #[cfg(windows)]
+                        {
+                            const MAIN_IPC_STARTUP_GRACE: Duration = Duration::from_secs(1);
+                            // Give the GUI time to arrange its replacement before forced takeover.
+                            std::thread::sleep(MAIN_IPC_STARTUP_GRACE);
+                            match crate::ipc::start("") {
+                                Ok(()) => return,
+                                Err(err) => log::error!("Failed to retry ipc startup: {err}"),
+                            }
+                        }
                         log::error!("ipc is occupied by another process, try kill it");
                         std::thread::spawn(stop_main_window_process).join().ok();
                     }
